host Vultr SEA NixOS VPS ai-jail pier (Daylight DC-1 hand) -- Eastern (EDT)
title Caravan dwell -- a standing quarrel says how long it has stood
prompt Keaton set the loop running: be Kyri in Radiant Style, read the operator card and the itineraries, close open agent-closable reds first, take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first, deep-read one council-rota doc, condense REMEMBER when a set closes, and send each finished increment as its own signed round.
think Standfast first. The living reds ledger reads five prose rows and every one of them closes -- %96 and %97 released on `20260820.030755`, %81, %83, and %84 closed before them, and the elder ranges folded to archive. Nothing agent-closable stood open, so the constructive queue was free.
think The running thread came from the newest log's recommend rather than from REMEMBER alone. relent had just landed: a quarrel its holder withdraws stops standing, on that holder's own word and on nobody else's. Its recommend named exactly what it left open -- what an operator does with a quarrel whose holder never returns, since only the raiser may take a note down and nothing in the arc weighs a silence that has lasted a hundred runs.
think The invariant bounded the answer before the design began. Seventy-one rungs hold one line: a supervisor may weigh a quarrel, report it, escort it, and carry it past itself, and it may never close one. So this rung cannot age a quarrel out, and it should not want to. What it can do is say how long -- which gives an operator the number the arc has never had while leaving the closing hand exactly where it belongs.
think The age had to be a fact about the quarrel rather than a finding of the run, and that decided the wire. It lives beside the standing note, which is the one record a provisioning already leaves alone, and it comes down inside `release_standing` -- so the age falls with the quarrel, and a position raised tomorrow begins at nothing, as every new quarrel should.
think Monotonicity is the rung's hard half. The runs a position stood through already happened, so a run reads the age on the wire before it writes and `DwellForgotten` refuses anything shorter -- otherwise a plan could look freshly objected-to by running often enough. The byte saturates at 255 rather than wrapping, which reads as *at least* 255 runs and never rolls a long quarrel back to nothing.
think The ordering is the mirror of relent's. The relenting is the first act of a run because the note it may take down is the note every step after it reads; the dwelling is the last, because a position has stood through this run only once the run is over -- and because the relenting above may already have taken down the very note an age would sit beside.
obs The rung was grown as a delegating tier over relent exactly as the arc has grown for seventy-one rungs: every elder fold re-exported unchanged, the report nested one deeper, and only this rung's own question local. It built clean on the first try and printed the finding on the first metal run.
obs One inherited check had to move rather than be worked around. relent's lap depends on a reader who accepts, so it asserts no position is carried forward; this lap depends on a reader who never returns, so both runs rightly carry one. The check was rewritten to require both runs identical at 1 -- the premise this rung studies -- rather than loosened.
obs The council rota doc this lap was item 18, `context/TWO_ROOMS.md`, taken as choir count 72 mod 27. It read as the right page for a rung about what a number tells a reader: a claim earns the checkable room only once a witness binds it, and every claim in this lap's prose is bound to a byte read back off the wire outside the run that wrote it.
obs `run_in_dwell` crossed the seventy-line ratchet by exactly one line -- the single `dwell: Dwell` parameter. The trim came out of a six-line comment that said the same thing in five, and the reasoning it carried moved into the function's own doc, where a reader wants it.
loom witness=caravan_dwell_witness rungs=72 phases=6 dependents=6 aged_undated=0 aged_dated=1 ageless_undated=1 ageless_dated=0 kept_both=1 heeded_both=1 wire_age=1
file caravan/dwell.rye the rung -- a standing quarrel says how many runs it has stood through, four refusals by name
file tools/caravan_dwell_witness.rish the witness -- the finding, the folds, the wire read outside the run, and five RED paths named
file tools/caravan_suite_witness.rish the choir gains its seventy-second rung
file caravan/README.md the durable entry for dwell, beside relent
file crux/REMEMBER.md the live edge moves to this rung; the prior one condenses to a pointer
recommend keep-going the arc now corrects a record, carries the correction, hears the answer, records the disagreement, escorts the word, bounds the objection, stands its standing, tells the raiser, reads their reply, carries a live quarrel past the run that heard it, makes the inheriting run answer for it, lets its holder close it, and finally says how long a standing one has stood -- so the question above is what an operator may ask of an age once they can read it: nothing in the arc yet lets a plan treat a quarrel of two runs differently from one of two hundred, and the honest next rung is whether a long-standing position earns a louder place in the record rather than a quieter one.
